  "notes": "Entry-level Blackwell consumer part. 12GB GDDR7 on 192-bit bus at 24 Gbps. 250W TGP. The 12GB VRAM is the critical constraint for local LLM inference - a 70B model at 4-bit quantization requires ~35GB, which exceeds this card's capacity. Suitable for models up to ~13B at 4-bit or ~7B at 8-bit. The RTX 5070 is the lowest-VRAM part in the 50-series and the first to be genuinely constrained by memory capacity rather than compute for LLM workloads.",
